# SoloBrief security response headers.
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the build output. Hugo copies
# static/ verbatim into public/, so static/_headers lands at public/_headers.
#
# Every comment is kept ABOVE the rule block on purpose. The rule block below is
# one contiguous run of "Name: value" lines with no blank lines and no inline
# comments, because a blank line terminates a rule in this file format and an
# indented comment is not guaranteed to be stripped inside one. A malformed line
# here fails silently: the site keeps serving, just with no security headers.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Added 2026-09-09 to close five High severity findings in the Lighthouse 13.4.1
# run of 2026-09-02: csp-xss, has-hsts, origin-isolation, clickjacking-mitigation
# and trusted-types-xss. All five are informative mode audits that score 1, so
# they never appeared in any failing audit list and none of them moves the Best
# Practices score of 77. Verified absent against the live server the same day:
# the only security headers solobrief.co sent were x-content-type-options and
# referrer-policy, and both are Cloudflare Pages defaults rather than ours.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security
#   One year. www.solobrief.co is the only subdomain that resolves and it already
#   answers 301 over HTTPS, so includeSubDomains costs nothing. preload is
#   deliberately omitted: it is close to irreversible (removal needs a browser
#   release cycle) and it only protects a browser's first ever request to us.
#
# X-Frame-Options
#   Chosen over CSP frame-ancestors because frame-ancestors is ignored by spec
#   when delivered in a Report-Only policy, and this change ships no enforcing
#   CSP. DENY rather than SAMEORIGIN: the built output contains zero same-origin
#   iframes, so we never frame ourselves. When the CSP goes enforcing, move to
#   frame-ancestors 'none' and delete this line rather than keeping both.
#
# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy
#   Safe here: a grep of the whole built site finds no window.open, so there is
#   no opener relationship to sever. Cookiebot uses an iframe, and COOP does not
#   affect iframes. COEP is deliberately NOT set: require-corp would break every
#   third party that does not send CORP (Google Fonts, Cookiebot, Clarity, gtag)
#   and the origin-isolation audit does not ask for it.
#
# X-Content-Type-Options
#   Cloudflare already sends this. Restated so the posture lives in the repo and
#   survives a move off Pages. A duplicate value is harmless for this header.
#
# Permissions-Policy
#   Only APIs nothing on this site can want. Deliberately NOT denied: fullscreen,
#   autoplay, clipboard-write, encrypted-media, picture-in-picture, accelerometer
#   and gyroscope. The YouTube facade injects an iframe that requests all seven,
#   and a document level denial cascades into the frame.
#
# Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only
#   REPORT ONLY, and it must stay that way until the reports have been read.
#   Origins came from the 41 network requests in the Lighthouse run plus a grep
#   of the built output, not from guesswork.
#   'unsafe-inline' in script-src is a real weakening and it is not optional
#   today: every page carries 8 to 11 inline scripts (announcement banner,
#   reading progress bar, sticky ToC, Clarity loader, gtag config, JSON-LD) and
#   every /go/ affiliate redirect page IS an inline script. Removing it needs per
#   block hashes or nonces, which is follow-up work, not this change. Until that
#   lands this policy does not stop XSS; it documents the real dependency graph
#   and catches anything new that appears outside it.
#   'unsafe-eval' is deliberately absent. If Cookiebot auto-blocking or Clarity
#   turns out to need it, the report will say so; do not add it pre-emptively.
#   require-trusted-types-for is deliberately absent. It would break Clarity and
#   gtag on contact. That is the trusted-types-xss finding, left open on purpose.
#
# HOW TO VERIFY, and this is not done yet
#   There is no reporting endpoint, so violations surface only in the browser
#   devtools console. Verification is a manual console pass over one page of each
#   type: home, a post with a YouTube facade, the calculator tool, a /go/ redirect
#   and the Kit signup. form-action and img-src are the two most likely to report
#   a false positive. Do not promote to enforcing on the absence of complaints.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://consent.cookiebot.com https://consentcdn.cookiebot.com https://www.clarity.ms https://scripts.clarity.ms https://www.googletagmanager.com https://solobrief.kit.com https://f.convertkit.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://*.cookiebot.com https://*.convertkit.com https://*.kit.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://i.ytimg.com https://*.cookiebot.com https://*.clarity.ms https://*.google-analytics.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://stats.g.doubleclick.net; connect-src 'self' https://*.cookiebot.com https://*.clarity.ms https://c.bing.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://stats.g.doubleclick.net https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.convertkit.com https://*.kit.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://consentcdn.cookiebot.com https://www.youtube.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; form-action 'self' https://*.convertkit.com https://*.kit.com
